Package: specrobust
Title: Specification-Robust Causal Inference in Observational Studies
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("Aditya", "Ghosh", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "ghoshadi@stanford.edu")
Description: Estimation and inference for the average treatment effect when
    several candidate covariate adjustment sets are plausible and it is not
    known which of them satisfies ignorability, as proposed by Ghosh and
    Rothenhaeusler (2025+). The population is reweighted, as little as
    possible in Kullback-Leibler divergence, so that every candidate estimand
    agrees, and the effect on that reweighted population is reported with a
    confidence interval that is valid as long as at least one candidate is
    valid and whose width shrinks at the parametric rate. Contrasts may be
    estimated by cross-fitted generalized random forests or by interacted
    linear regression, and any known function of the shared covariates may be
    protected from the reweighting.
